Runtime coverage
The two-workspace package fixtures mount production plugin entry points over harness seams. They verify model options received by the spawn adapter, host-authenticated HTTP routing, the target JSONC bytes, and the rebuilt Web client's request and form behavior. The separately run pinned DSH model-config-live-refresh case is recorded at ../../skill-tests/model-config-live.json. It records a genuine child moving from deepseek-v4-flash to deepseek-v4-pro on the same boot after a host settings save. The isolated runtime case uses one workspace. The package tests exercise two workspaces and run the card without a rendered browser.

Documentation follow-up
The user guide §7.2, TUI guide §3.1/§6.2 and bundle/config package READMEs now describe the same distinction as the rebuilt Web disclosure. Web model fields save to the selected session's project, while general Web settings and the TUI's entry form save profile-wide values. The earlier mounted host-entry experiment demonstrates the latter path. Both language editions were updated without changing runtime sources.
